    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_534cff38e31b712de8954ef4b78d94c8d42e89d9c653a766cd4860ecbee01a41",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source gives two complementary prime/zero representations: prime powers index the Gutzwiller-like oscillations of the zero density, with logarithms of prime powers playing action-like roles, while zero-indexed oscillations reconstruct the prime-power density and the phase of log zeta supplies a shared analytic bridge. That two-way relation does not make Riemann's prime-density formula a dynamical trace formula: its zero-labelled terms have no repetition indices, the implied trajectories are not periodic, their amplitudes have no zero-index dependence, and the smooth contribution from trivial zeros cannot be absorbed into Thomas-Fermi data.",
